# Mutual Exclusion, Semaphore and Monitor

## Use Case
### Concurrent Seat Booking System

This project demonstrates synchronization mechanisms used in a
concurrent seat booking system where multiple users may try to book
the same seats simultaneously.

## Programs

### 1. Mutex
Demonstrates mutual exclusion by allowing only one thread to access
the shared booking resource at a time.

### 2. Mutex and Semaphore
Uses mutex and semaphore mechanisms to control concurrent access
to shared resources.

### 3. Mutex, Semaphore and Monitor
Demonstrates synchronization using mutex, semaphore and monitor
concepts for safe concurrent seat booking.

## Concepts Used
- Threads
- Mutual Exclusion
- Mutex
- Semaphore
- Monitor
- Critical Section
- Process Synchronization
- Race Condition
